TASK_QUEUE.md-108-| FROZEN-RECEIPT-CONSTANT-STALE-01 | P2 Next Slice | 2026-08-27 | Stop successor-family PACK_AUTHENTICATION from resting on `CURRENT_FROZEN_RECEIPT_SHA256`, the generator constant that names the PREDECESSOR's freeze receipt | No phase exit-checklist matrix row exists. Landed on PR #214 (branch `fix/packauth-soundness-rows`; gauntlet: design consult → implementation → independent audit → fix round → delta re-audit). The staleness is structural, not an accident: `embedded_generator_bytes()` emits a successor generator by substituting only `CURRENT_FAMILY_SUFFIX`, so every successor family is born one generation behind and `_v4` — emitted from the `_v3` generators — will name the `_v2` freeze-0002 digest too. Executed across all nine packs (`docs/process_traces/2026-08-26-t26-s3/characterization.md`, replayable via `replay-characterization.sh`): the three ordinal-1 packs match their own receipt and pass a bare `--check`; all six successors exit 1 with `generation failed: the current frozen identity requires preserve mode`. ADOPTED RULING: the constant is NOT refreshed per generation and the authentication path stops depending on it. Refreshing is impossible rather than merely undesirable — a successor generator is emitted before its own freeze receipt exists, so the digest it would need does not yet exist, and editing the generator after the mint would change already-frozen pack bytes (D-153 would then force a new family generation). The ruling is recorded normatively in `docs/contracts/receipt_histsem_verifier.md` §'Adopted A93 ruling' (dated 2026-08-26) and pinned by `test_frozen_receipt_constant_variants_do_not_change_the_authentication_verdict`, which holds one derivation fixed, varies the constant through absent / matches-current / names-predecessor / unrelated / computed / duplicated / malformed forms and requires an IDENTICAL authentication verdict with only diagnostic differences. The constant is now read by a TOTAL `ast.parse`/`ast.literal_eval` extractor that never raises and never reaches the verdict; its relation is recorded with `authentication_dependency: false`. An earlier shape that refused a flagless generator merely because the constant existed was caught by the independent audit (F1, blocker) and removed — preserve CAPABILITY, not the constant, now selects the invocation. NOT done here: PACKAUTH-PRESERVE-TAUTOLOGY-01, which shares the branch and stays open on the delta re-audit's D1 blocker. A binding `docs/decision_log.md` entry for this ruling is OWED at the merge gate (magistrate's act). |
TASK_QUEUE.md:109:| MINT-CHECKOUT-DECLARATION-01 | P2 Next Slice | 2026-08-27 | Build the mint-time measurement-checkout declaration check that D-154 R-3 re-sites the locality lens onto, so the one real event the absolute pack_root comparison ever caught is caught once, at mint, against a declared checkout | No phase exit-checklist matrix row exists. Merged via #208 (squash SHA to be recorded at merge): `generate_freeze_receipt` takes a REQUIRED keyword-only `measurement_checkout`, and both production CLIs (`scripts/generate_arm_readiness.py freeze`, `scripts/author_arm_readiness_evidence.py`) take a required `--measurement-checkout`; the gate compares the resolved repository owning the pack against the strictly-resolved declaration, fires on the CREATE path only (after idempotent replay returns, so R-3's "once, AT MINT" holds) and before any byte is written (so a refusal spends no freeze ordinal). New reason code `readiness_r1_measurement_checkout` (role `MEASUREMENT_CHECKOUT`, type `CUSTODY`) with its ninth ruled-registry `refusal_vocabulary` entry; load-closure pinned in BOTH directions and the `READINESS_REASON_CODES` census moved 55 → 56 deliberately. All four acceptance items VERIFIED by an independent read-only audit: refuse-outside/mint-inside, two-directional registry closure, a T10 `wtTXN`-class regression across two real git repositories through the real CLI by subprocess (exact reason code, and proof no receipt namespace was created), and supplied-never-inferred (no env var, `window.env`, cwd, `REPO_ROOT`, or pack-derived fallback exists on the declared side). Mutation kills recorded for the gate, both closure directions, and the gate PLACEMENT (moving it above the replay branch goes red). The live `docs/phase_2/window_runbook.md` freeze command was repaired in the same PR; ten dated historical command records were deliberately left unchanged. NOT done here, on the record: the transaction runbook's PROMPT 4–6 text (`docs/process_traces/2026-08-22-t20/real-transaction-runbook.md` is pinned to reviewed head `3c96b18f`, so the delta is REPORTED in the PR body and is the magistrate's to land), and C7's clone-based pre-mint refusal screen, RULED by the magistrate: the sacrificial check declares the THROWAWAY CLONE'S OWN PATH, because the declaration binds the checkout performing the freeze and for that step the performing checkout is the clone. The author-CLI scope expansion (adding the required --measurement-checkout to scripts/author_arm_readiness_evidence.py, whose _parser() carried a prior "--pack-root-only" note) is RATIFIED: that note rules out an INERT step-6 digest flag and cannot forbid a required one, without which the emitted freeze command dies at argparse. Registry blast radius measured twice independently: the entry moves the registry SHA-256 `7a164213…` → `cf6deaae…`, all nine committed freeze receipts already bind registry v1 (`d248fdc5…`) and so add no new casualty, and the magistrate RULED the sequencing: #208 merges BEFORE the `_v4` mint, in the same pre-mint wave as W-10 (#209) and S11 (#213), so the `_v4` receipts mint against the NEW registry SHA `cf6deaae…` and estate 11 covers all three together — no receipt ever refuses on registry mismatch. |
TASK_QUEUE.md-110-| ARM-PACKROOT-COMPARISON-01 | P2 Next Slice | 2026-08-27 | Extend the D-154 R-1/R-2 truthfulness cure to the arm side so the arm-side pack comparisons stop reporting a content difference when only the recorded pack location differs | No phase exit-checklist matrix row exists. Merged via #208 (squash SHA to be recorded at merge): the R-1 freeze-replay comparator was generalised into one shared helper, `_pack_mapping_mismatch_kind`, and both arm-side whole-dict equalities now route through it — the dry-run staleness limb and the consumed-arm authentication in the launch-lineage check — with `pack_root` compared under the same successor-scoped rule (generations ≥ `family_publication_first_generation` repository-relative and still COMPARED, `_v3` and earlier absolute per the 2026-08-20 ruling, lexical validation only, no normcase, non-repo paths still refusing). Details are true per branch; no new reason codes. All four acceptance items met, with mutation kills recorded at both named sites. The independent audit REFUTED the first round on a finding the row's own registration missed: a THIRD whole-record `_pack_record` comparison in `_derive_arm_semantics_for_verification` is production-active via `scripts/launch_window.py` → `_verify_arm_receipt` and DOMINATED both cured sites, so the cure was unobservable through the real launcher. Confirmed at the bench, cured in the last code commit of the series, and ADOPTED by the magistrate: a whole-dict site that DOMINATES both cured sites must be cured or the cure is unreachable through the launcher. The fence's "only the two arm-side comparisons" was the registering sweep's CENSUS, not a limit — the PR #192 refuter found two consumers of the recorded absolute pack_root and this row's audit corrected that census to FOUR (freeze identity, dry-run staleness, arm verification, consumed-arm authentication), all now routed through the single shared helper. The delta re-audit's independent census confirms the comparison-site set is now CLOSED at four sites, all through the one helper. NOT proven, by the PR's own record: alias-free relocation end to end (the strict `resolve(strict=True)` guard refuses it earlier by design, so the launcher regression retains the original path as a symlink), live boot-session acquisition, and real family-publication marker replay — the end-to-end test patches `_current_boot_session_id` because the sandbox denies `/usr/sbin/sysctl` and installs a synthetic successor route that bypasses `_gate_family_publication`; neither patch can bypass the pack comparator. |
TASK_QUEUE.md:111:| CONSUME-CONFIRMATION-SUPPLY-01 | P1 Phase Gate | 2026-08-27 | Give the consume lane a step-6 confirmation supply line so the real transaction's consume-side C-to-S gate can enforce the operator-confirmed step-6 digest | No phase exit-checklist matrix row exists. Merged via #204 (`318f5a70`). The row's goal prose named `scripts/generate_arm_readiness.py`'s `consume` subcommand; that subcommand is RETIRED (unconditional `readiness_usage_invalid` pointing at `scripts/launch_window.py`, pinned by `test_standalone_consume_cli_is_retired_with_launcher_guidance`), so options added there would forward to nothing and would advertise a second consume route that does not exist — the independent audit agreed with leaving it unchanged. The real gap was one lane over: `scripts/launch_window.py` accepted `--expected-confirmation-digest` but had no route for the TABLE PATH, which was only ever auto-resolved to `<custody>/family_publication/d117_step6_confirmation_table_v4.json` inside `_derive_arm_semantics_for_verification` — the same 3e signature PR #188 (`f82247ee`) cured for `freeze`. Cure: `--step6-confirmation-table`, forwarded at all four sites that already forward the digest (`_verify_arm_receipt` in assembly; `_consume_launch_capability` and `verify_consumed_launch` in launch; `verify_consumed_launch` in lifecycle `start`); omitting it passes `None` exactly as today, so every existing refusal and the auto-resolution stay byte-identical. Acceptance: seven regressions in `tests/test_launch_window.py` — legs A-F (valid pair at a deliberately NON-default table location, missing path, missing digest, malformed digest, mismatched bytes, nothing supplied) plus `test_launch_cli_real_chain_reaches_confirmation_authenticator`, which drives the REAL `main()` -> `_verify_arm_receipt` -> `_derive_arm_semantics_for_verification` chain down to a spy at `_authenticate_confirmation_table` and pins both the explicit path and the preserved auto-resolution. Because missing