docs/decision_log.md-186-| D-159 | FROZEN-RECEIPT CONSTANT IS NEVER REFRESHED (A93 FROZEN-RECEIPT-CONSTANT-STALE-01 ruling; Sol xhigh design seat out-designed the lead's sketch; magistrate 2026-08-27; custody `docs/process_traces/2026-08-26-t26-s3/`, normative text in `docs/contracts/receipt_histsem_verifier.md` §"Adopted A93 ruling"): a successor generator is emitted BEFORE its own freeze receipt exists, so the digest a refreshed `CURRENT_FROZEN_RECEIPT_SHA256` would need does not yet exist; the constant therefore names the predecessor by construction and is not an authentication input. Hard-refusing a stale constant detects nothing at §3.4 (no receipt yet) and mass-refuses after §3.6. RULING: the constant never gates authentication (pinned by `test_frozen_receipt_constant_variants_do_not_change_the_authentication_verdict`); ordinal-1 packs match their own receipt and pass a bare `--check`; every successor exits 1 with `the current frozen identity requires preserve mode` (nine-pack executed matrix). NO frozen bytes changed; no re-mint; `_v4` mint re-verified (§3.4 projected authorship PASS, histsem PASS via anchor+replay, +2.2 s per gate). A94 PACKAUTH-PRESERVE-TAUTOLOGY-01 stays OPEN on delta blocker D1 (flagless-generator preserve detection is a name scan; cure = default-deny flagless generators except a closed reviewed-digest allowlist, pinned at both boundaries; unreachable by any in-repo generator, so `_v4` unaffected). | adopted (magistrate; PR #214) |
