docs/decision_log.md:4603:     operator supersession artifact (append-only, hash-sealed, naming the
     1	# Research-question coverage against the frozen `_v5` campaign, the transfer fiducial (known-gap diagnostic), and the three-model ladder
     2	
     3	**Date:** 2026-08-28
     4	
     5	This is the coverage map Ed requested and decision D-163 (the ruling on what follows `_v5`: the inserted-gap fiducial and the three-model decode ladder) ordered (`docs/decision_log.md:10336-10348`). It puts every live row in `docs/research_question_registry.md` beside the additional identifiers retained only in `docs/research_question_bank.md`, then asks what the frozen `_v5` campaign on `mlx-community/Qwen3-1.7B-4bit` and `mlx-community/Qwen3-8B-4bit`, the first post-campaign transfer-fiducial diagnostic, the three-model ladder whose D-163 model set is unresolved under `_v5`, or evidence already retained at the desk can honestly answer. The live registry supplies current type, status, and claim ceiling; the bank supplies the historical question wording, rejected upgrades, and the ten identifiers that were folded into live rows rather than given their own registry rows.
     6	
     7	Here, a large language model (LLM) has two measured stages: **prefill**, which processes the prompt, and **decode**, which emits output tokens. MLX is Apple’s open-source machine-learning framework and is the inference runtime used here. Apple’s `powermetrics` program samples modeled central-processing-unit (CPU), graphics-processing-unit (GPU), and Apple Neural Engine (ANE) on-chip power channels, called **rails**, for the system on a chip (SoC); these are not physical wall measurements. Its **sampler cadence** is how often it writes a power record, about every tenth of a second here. A **cell resolution bound**, called a detection floor in the artifacts, is the largest false energy difference the named measurement system can manufacture for one fixed condition. An **A/B/B/A block** is a counterbalanced four-run order whose first and last runs use condition A and whose middle two use condition B.
     8	
     9	A **bundle** is the per-run evidence folder—power trace, events, outputs, and metadata—that the reducer, the analysis program, consumes. A **holdout** or **held-out request** is deliberately excluded from fitting and used only to test prediction. A **smoke run** is a small feasibility test, and a **shim** is a small adapter between the external runner and JouleWise. Greedy, sampled, and beam decoding are output-selection strategies: greedy always chooses the most probable next token, sampling draws randomly, and beam decoding keeps several candidate continuations. HumanEval is a public code-generation benchmark of programming problems; FLORES is a public multilingual translation benchmark that presents the same sentences in many languages; and **tokenizer fertility** means the number of tokens produced per word or character for a language. AXI names the project’s architecture-extension stream. A state-space/attention hybrid combines recurrent state updates with attention layers, rather than using attention alone.
    10	
    11	## How to read the tables
    12	
    13	The registry/bank status is copied, not reconsidered: **promoted** means the question owns a named project slot; **banked** means viable but not promoted; **candidate** means proposed and bounded; **killed** means deliberately rejected; **answered-L1** means answered only at the registry’s limited descriptive claim level; and **candidate (C-023)** is the whole-project review’s candidate class.
    14	
    15	Every coverage cell uses exactly one of these labels. The letter is only a reading aid; the words are controlling.
    16	
    17	- **A. `answered by _v5`** — the frozen three-pack design on `mlx-community/Qwen3-1.7B-4bit` and `mlx-community/Qwen3-8B-4bit` will answer the row if collection and governed close-out succeed.
    18	- **B. `answerable by fiducial`** — the diagnostic `TRANSFER-FIDUCIAL-01` post-campaign window will answer the row. It is not eligible to support a claim and cannot create or widen one.
    19	- **C. `answerable by ladder`** — the D-163 decode-only 0.5B/1.5B/7B ladder as ruled predates D-164, and its model set is unresolved under `_v5` (`docs/decision_log.md:191`).
    20	- **D. `answerable at the desk now`** — retained evidence already supports an answer at the row’s stated ceiling. “Partial” means the artifact answers only the named subpart, not the whole row.
    21	- **E. `not answerable with this instrument`** — the present M3 Max, `powermetrics` rails, and software boundary cannot physically reach the answer. The short reason names the structural limit: another device or meter, an unmeasured endpoint, a runtime that cannot run here, an event faster than the sampler cadence, or a killed question.
    22	- **F. `not a question`** — an application idea or methodology artifact is built, used, proposed, or killed rather than answered as a research question. The state is stated in the same cell.
    23	- **G. `answerable with this instrument, no route scheduled`** — this Mac, sampler, bundle format, and floor machinery could answer the row, but `_v5`, the fiducial, the ladder, and retained desk evidence do not. The short reason states the additional cells and measurement night or nights required.
    24	- **H. `answerable by the _v6 scored leg`** — Ed’s scored benchmark leg uses GSM8K, eight items per member, and a pinned checker; accuracy is a set property under the AP-5 / C5-1.9 quarantine because training-data contamination cannot be ruled out. It is built at the desk during `_v5` and run post-campaign after the fiducial night (`docs/decision_log.md:193`).
    25	
    26	The `_v5` rows below cite the checked-in `*_v3` predecessor pack shapes. The contrast pack has a checked-in **analysis manifest**—the predeclared instructions for reducing and testing its data—at `configs/campaigns/d117_contrast_qwen25_1p5b_vs_7b_v3/analysis_manifest_v3.json`; the two floor directories have plan trees but no `analysis_manifest_v3.json`. No separately named `_v5` pack configuration or fifth-generation freeze record was found in this worktree. The predecessor `_v4` project task record and final ruling say that the real transaction would have created freeze records from these three predecessor campaign families (`docs/process/state_kernel.json:4500-4548`; `docs/process_traces/2026-08-20-go-session/rulings-r5-consolidation.md:72-104`), but D-164 says `_v4` is never collected. The `_v5` pack re-pins the models to `mlx-community/Qwen3-1.7B-4bit` and `mlx-community/Qwen3-8B-4bit` per D-164 and is not yet in this tree (`docs/decision_log.md:191`). The checked-in program that validates manifest generation is `joulewise/analysis_manifest_v3.py`.
    27	
