./docs/paper/round7/structural-edits.md-80-**Worked retained-fixture pass (fixture evidence, not a round-7 campaign result):** In retained block `b01`, \(\delta_1=z_1=0.2146256513\) J. The onset sweep runs from \(0.1098764207\) to \(0.2243993676\) J and the offset sweep from \(0.0576055478\) to \(0.3349382543\) J, so \(d_1^-=-0.2617693342\) J, \(d_1^+=0.1300863192\) J, and \(q_1=0.2617693342\) J after outward rounding. Its four residual half-widths are \(0.0015589205\), \(0.0337198644\), \(0.0491358083\), and \(0.0127439131\) J, giving \(\ell_1=0.0485792531\) J. The retained second block gives \(q_2=0.6153099135\) J and \(\ell_2=0.1356776459\) J. Enumerating the two shared signs and four local-sign combinations produces a point comparative unguarded floor of \(2.4305766103\) J and a maximum shared-error unguarded floor of \(8.8304376431\) J, hence \(R_{cm}=8.8304376431/2.4305766103=3.6330628732\), which passes the threshold of 2. These numbers come from `tests/fixtures/fcm_r4_real_blocks/measured_pair.json` and demonstrate the registered arithmetic only.
./docs/paper/round7/structural-edits.md-81-
./docs/paper/round7/structural-edits.md-82-Absolute rows do not report this comparative replay as though it were a measurement. They print `not_applicable`: the registered absolute estimator first subtracts its cell mean, so under the replay's stated idealization that one shared fiducial timing error displaces every observation uniformly, that displacement cancels exactly. This cancellation is the reason for `not_applicable`, not evidence that a shared timing error is physically absent.
